Z||000000||kanada||04-24-2001||08:57 PM||||i've reacently purchased a v6 engine out of a fiero to replace my v6.  the engine is complete (starter intact, brackets, injectors, etc...)  because i don't have access to a hoist, i'm having it done in a garage<P>i was wondering if anyone knew the approximate time it would take to exchange the engine<P>bare in mind that i'm also replacing the transmission so the engine and transmission can be taken out as a whole||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-24-2001||09:13 PM||||We removed a 2.8 with 145,000 miles on it out of an 87 GT and installed a 21,000 mile 2.8 into it. We used the same trans (5-spd) and replaced all bushings and mounts with poly, tuned up engine, replaced clutch, and the suspension (struts/springs). Total time with 3 guys was 14 hours. We did use a hoist. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||04-25-2001||04:55 PM||||I've done it over a weekend. I did use a cherry picker though<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-25-2001||05:07 PM||||By your saying that you are having it done "in a garage", I'm assuming that you mean you are paying someoe to do it.  A professional shop <I>should</I> be able to turn it out in an afternoon. However, since Murphy's Law will prove that all their bays are currently filled with cars that require backordered parts, two of their mechanics have the flu, and their pet samoyed ran away and evryone is distraught, you can count on them having your car for at least a month.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
